Yes — and your instinct here is correct. The next step is **UI structure first, AI sophistication second**. If the interface cannot express the information properly, improving the AI will not improve the user experience. Right now your backend already produces useful signals (topic, urgency, deadline, score), but the UI treats them like **tags on a message**, not like **structured academic context**.

The better sequence is:

First build the **information architecture of the UI** so it can express richer context.
Then improve the AI so it can populate those fields more accurately.

If you reverse this order, you will keep adding smarter models but the user will still see the same flat feed.

