### About multi-model orchestration

Yes — and this is actually the direction systems like this naturally evolve toward.

Right now your AI pipeline is essentially:

```
Email → LLM → Labels + Summary
```

Later it can become something like:

```
Email
   ↓
Preprocessing
   ↓
Classification model
   ↓
Extraction model
   ↓
Reasoning model
   ↓
Academic context engine
```

Different models can do different jobs:

Classification model
Determines topic and urgency.

Extraction model
Pulls structured data like course name, instructor, dates.

Reasoning model
Decides what action the student needs to take.

Summarization model
Generates the UI summary.

This is called **pipeline orchestration**, and it scales better than asking one LLM to do everything.

